IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-nouns`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- PART 2 (Prisoners): regulations 2 and 3.
-- Source: plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-04-06 (uksi-2015-173.txt); not the official text.
--
-- One relation: the person and the Secretary of State, over whether a state pension is to be paid for a day.
-- For a day on which the person is a prisoner, the person has no claim to payment (and the Secretary of State has
-- no duty to pay); regulation 3 takes a remand out of that until a sentence is later imposed.
-- The unit is one day of the person's custody (regulation 2(1) speaks of "any period during which").

§ `Part 2 -- Prisoners`

§§ `Regulation 2(2) and (3): who is a prisoner`

-- src:29 | (2) Except where paragraph (3) applies, a person is a prisoner for the purposes of paragraph (1) where the person is—
-- src:30 | (a) a prisoner in Great Britain or elsewhere who is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings;
-- src:31 | (b) a prisoner in Great Britain or elsewhere who is unlawfully at large;
-- src:32 | (c) a prisoner in Great Britain who is being detained—
-- src:33 | (i) under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983 (removal to hospital of persons serving sentences of imprisonment etc) ; and
-- src:34 | (ii) on or before the day which the Secretary of State certifies to be the person's release date (if any) within the meaning in section 50(3) of that Act ;
-- src:35 | (d) a prisoner in Great Britain who is being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 (transfer of prisoners for treatment of mental disorder) .
-- src:36 | (3) Where a person outside Great Britain is a prisoner within paragraph (2)(a) or (b) and, in similar circumstances in Great Britain, the person would not have been a prisoner, the person is not a prisoner within paragraph (2)(a) or (b).
@ref Regulation 2(2), 2(3) (src:29-36)
GIVEN `that day` IS A `A day of a person's custody`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph (3) of regulation 2 applies on the day` `that day` MEANS
        (NOT `that day`'s `in Great Britain`)
    AND (    `that day`'s `the kind of custody` EQUALS `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings`
          OR `that day`'s `the kind of custody` EQUALS `unlawfully at large`)
    AND `that day`'s `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner`

-- Paragraph (2)(c)(ii): "on or before the day which the Secretary of State certifies to be the person's release date (if any)".
-- The certification is the Secretary of State's, so it is an input. Where there is no certified date ("if any"),
-- nothing ends the detention under section 47 and the condition is taken as met (fork F4).
@ref Regulation 2(2)(c)(ii) (src:34)
GIVEN `that day` IS A `A day of a person's custody`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day is on or before the certified release date, if there is one` `that day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `that day`'s `the release date the Secretary of State has certified`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST certified THEN Day (`that day`'s `the day`) AT MOST Day certified

@ref Regulation 2(2) (src:29-35)
GIVEN `that day` IS A `A day of a person's custody`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` `that day` MEANS
        (NOT `paragraph (3) of regulation 2 applies on the day` `that day`)
    AND (    `that day`'s `the kind of custody` EQUALS `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings`
          OR `that day`'s `the kind of custody` EQUALS `unlawfully at large`
          OR (    `that day`'s `the kind of custody` EQUALS `detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983`
              AND `that day`'s `in Great Britain`
              AND `the day is on or before the certified release date, if there is one` `that day`)
          OR (    `that day`'s `the kind of custody` EQUALS `detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`
              AND `that day`'s `in Great Britain`))

§§ `Regulation 3: a person remanded in custody`

-- src:40 | (2) Subject to paragraph (3), the described sentences for the purposes of paragraph (1) are—
-- src:41 | (a) a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings;
-- src:42 | (b) a sentence of detention where the provisions mentioned in regulation 2(2)(c)(i) or (d) apply;
-- src:43 | (c) a suspended sentence within the meaning in section 286 of the Sentencing Code (suspended sentences of imprisonment).
-- src:44 | (3) A sentence described in paragraph (2)(a) which is imposed outside Great Britain is not a described sentence for the purposes of paragraph (1) if, in similar circumstances in Great Britain, a sentence described in paragraph (2)(a) would not have been imposed.
@ref Regulation 3(2), 3(3) (src:40-44)
GIVEN `the sentence` IS A `Sentence imposed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the sentence is one described in regulation 3(2)` `the sentence` MEANS
        (    `the sentence`'s `its kind` EQUALS `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings`
         AND (NOT (    `the sentence`'s `it was imposed outside Great Britain`
                   AND `the sentence`'s `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed`)))
    OR  `the sentence`'s `its kind` EQUALS `a sentence of detention where the provisions mentioned in regulation 2(2)(c)(i) or (d) apply`
    OR  `the sentence`'s `its kind` EQUALS `a suspended sentence within the meaning in section 286 of the Sentencing Code`

-- src:39 | (1) Where a person is remanded in custody for an offence, regulation 2(1) does not apply unless a sentence described in paragraph (2) is later imposed on the person for the offence.
@ref Regulation 3(1) (src:39)
GIVEN `that day` IS A `A day of a person's custody`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 2(1) does not apply to the day because of regulation 3` `that day` MEANS
        `that day`'s `remanded in custody for an offence`
    AND (CONSIDER `that day`'s `the sentence later imposed for that offence`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST sentence THEN (NOT `the sentence is one described in regulation 3(2)` sentence))

§§ `Regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid`

-- src:28 | (1) Subject to regulation 3, a person is not to be paid a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act (state pension) for any period during which the person is a prisoner who is mentioned in paragraph (2).
@ref Regulation 2(1) (src:28)
GIVEN `that day` IS A `A day of a person's custody`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a state pension is not to be paid for the day` `that day` MEANS
        `the person is a prisoner within regulation 2(2) on the day` `that day`
    AND (NOT `regulation 2(1) does not apply to the day because of regulation 3` `that day`)

§§ `Regulation 2(4): relevant benefits`

-- Regulation 2(4) is a single statement about the interpretation of another provision: in determining rights to
-- "relevant benefits" (a term of the parent Act, not among the inputs) for regulation 2, regulation 13 "shall not
-- have effect". Encoded as the one thing it says (fork F5).
-- src:37 | (4) In determining a person’s rights to relevant benefits for the purposes of this regulation, regulation 13 of the State Pension Regulations 2015 (minimum number of qualifying years), and any provisions in Northern Ireland which correspond to that regulation, shall not have effect.
@ref Regulation 2(4) (src:37)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 13 has effect when determining rights to relevant benefits for regulation 2` MEANS FALSE
